meta {
  name: Update Alert Rule
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/alerts/{{alert_id}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

body:json {
  {
    "enabled": false,
    "expression": "cpu.usage_percent > 90",
    "for_duration_secs": 600
  }
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt_token}}
}

docs {
  Partial update — every field is optional, omitted fields keep their
  current value. `description: null` explicitly clears the description.

  Body fields (all optional):
    name, description, enabled, expression, severity,
    for_duration_secs, eval_interval_secs, cooldown_secs,
    silenced_until

  `silenced_until` is an absolute unix-epoch timestamp (or null to clear).
  Prefer `POST/DELETE /alerts/{id}/silence` when the intent is just to
  silence the rule — those endpoints take a relative `duration_secs`,
  skip expression revalidation, and won't accidentally stomp a concurrent
  full-rule edit.

  Server re-runs full validation against the merged result, so an
  invalid expression or out-of-range duration after the merge fails
  the request without partially mutating the row.

  ⚠ Hot-reload note: changing the expression / interval / for_duration
  on an already-running rule does NOT re-bounce the evaluator task
  today — the change only takes effect on next server restart. Coming
  in a follow-up; flagged here so you don't think a rule went stale.

  Errors:
    400 BAD_REQUEST — invalid expression or range
    404 NOT_FOUND   — id doesn't exist
}
